AltiVec (VMX) for simdjson's "ppc64" kernel, for the +altivec variant.

Upstream builds the ppc64 kernel only for 64-bit PowerPC with VSX/POWER8
(portability.h requires __PPC64__, __ALTIVEC__ and __POWER8_VECTOR__) and
its simd.h uses VSX-only operations (vec_vsx_ld/st, vbpermq, 2x64-bit
vectors).  This patch:

- portability.h, isadetection.h: recognise PowerPC under every macro
  spelling (Darwin compilers define __ppc__/__ppc64__, never
  __PPC__/__PPC64__) and enable the kernel on any PowerPC with AltiVec,
  including 32-bit, where it also defines SIMDJSON_IS_32BITS.  Without
  AltiVec nothing changes: the portable fallback kernel is used.
- ppc64/simd.h: plain-AltiVec replacements behind __VSX__ /
  __POWER8_VECTOR__ guards (POWER7+ code generation is unchanged):
  to_bitmask as bit weights + vec_msum, unaligned loads as the
  lvx/lvsl/vperm idiom (reads only the two aligned lines holding the 16
  bytes, so it stays inside SIMDJSON_PADDING), stores through an aligned
  temporary, compress masks from the thintable halves.
- ppc64/numberparsing_defs.h: full_multiplication for 32-bit non-MSVC
  compilers (the kernel otherwise calls the MSVC-only _umul128 there) and
  __builtin_bswap64 where neither byteswap.h nor sys/endian.h exists.

Written for this port (2026-09, rebased onto 5.1.1); upstream CI never
runs big-endian PowerPC, so the test suite (+tests) is the validation.

diff -ru include/simdjson/portability.h include/simdjson/portability.h
--- include/simdjson/portability.h
+++ include/simdjson/portability.h
@@ -86,9 +86,24 @@
 
 
 #endif
-#elif defined(__PPC64__) || defined(_M_PPC64)
+#elif defined(__PPC64__) || defined(_M_PPC64) || defined(__ppc64__) ||         \
+    defined(__powerpc64__) ||                                                  \
+    ((defined(__PPC__) || defined(__ppc__) || defined(_ARCH_PPC)) &&           \
+     defined(__ALTIVEC__))
+// Covers 64-bit PowerPC under every macro spelling (Darwin compilers define
+// __ppc64__, not __PPC64__), plus 32-bit PowerPC with AltiVec: the "ppc64"
+// kernel only needs 128-bit vectors and 64-bit scalar arithmetic, both of
+// which 32-bit PowerPC provides.  32-bit PowerPC without AltiVec falls
+// through to the generic 32-bit fallback below.
 #define SIMDJSON_IS_PPC64 1
-#if defined(__ALTIVEC__) && defined(__POWER8_VECTOR__)
+#if !(defined(__PPC64__) || defined(_M_PPC64) || defined(__ppc64__) ||         \
+      defined(__powerpc64__))
+#define SIMDJSON_IS_PPC_32BITS 1
+#define SIMDJSON_IS_32BITS 1
+#endif
+// The kernel's VSX/POWER8 operations have plain-AltiVec replacements
+// (ppc64/simd.h), so AltiVec alone is enough.
+#if defined(__ALTIVEC__)
 #define SIMDJSON_IS_PPC64_VMX 1
 #endif // defined(__ALTIVEC__)
 #else
